  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1em; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/180788/rss" title="devblogs.microsoft.com" style=" color: #3366aa;    font-size: 1.05em;"&gt;Announcing TypeScript 6.0 Beta&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — v6.0 is largely a &lt;em&gt;“time to clean up your tsconfig”&lt;/em&gt; release, designed to bridge the transition to the &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/180789/rss" style=" color: #3366aa;   "&gt;Go-powered native TypeScript 7&lt;/a&gt; later this year. Be aware of some tweaks, like &lt;code&gt;types&lt;/code&gt; defaulting to &lt;code&gt;[]&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;--strict&lt;/code&gt; now being true by default, among &lt;a href="https://javascriptweekly.com/link/180790/rss" style=" color: #3366aa;   "&gt;many more breaking changes and deprecations.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Microsoft &lt;/p&gt;
